# 20 - Testing Readiness
Provide repeatable tests that validate core behavior without production services.

## Applicable Rules
You must follow [`00-execution-policy.mdc`](./00-execution-policy.mdc), [`testing.mdc`](../.cursor/testing.mdc), [`ci_cd_quality_gates.mdc`](../.cursor/ci_cd_quality_gates.mdc), [`state_management.mdc`](../.cursor/state_management.mdc), and [`layouts.mdc`](../.cursor/layouts.mdc).

## Implementation
1. Create test helpers for app setup and provider overrides.
2. Add tests for validators, mappers, responsive utilities, themes, and shared components.
3. Add shell tests covering mobile and desktop layout decisions.
4. Add a startup/navigation integration smoke test when host tooling supports it.
5. Document test commands.
6. Tests must not call production services.

## Acceptance Criteria
- `flutter test` must pass.
- Important shared UI and responsive behavior must have coverage.
- Test helpers and baseline unit/widget tests must exist.
- Integration tests may be host-dependent but must remain documented.
